    "created_at": "2019-08-23T07:04:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-23T07:04:57Z",
    "body": "Hey folks,\r\n\r\nWhile trying to fix this, I discovered that it's going to be a lot harder than I initially suspected because of some issues in how the code is structured right now. There's no way to get printing flags from the argument parser to the printing code without using something icky, like a global variable or envar.\r\n\r\n@yonkeltron  I can put up a tiny patch that should solve your issue in day-to-day usage (it'll define `STARSHIP_SHELL=fish` in the fish init code so that if you launch `fish` from `zsh`, you no longer get the funky character prompts). After that, the only failure case I know of should be when manually running `starship prompt` or `starship module`. Those can be fixed by disabling the `STARSHIP_SHELL` envar for that command, i.e.\r\n\r\n```\r\nSTARSHIP_SHELL=\"\" starship prompt <flags>\r\n```\r\n\r\nDoes anyone have a use case affected by this issue that can't be solved by the above patch + workaround? If not, I'd like to defer work on this until after the v1.0 refactor (stay tuned for details!), since it should be much easier to correct at that point.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
